The attached image displays confocal microscopy images of skeletal muscle injection sites 24 hours after intramuscular injection, providing visual evidence of Nano-11's effect on local inflammation and cellular uptake. The top row illustrates the injection site of AF647-labeled Nano-11 with OVA, showing significant recruitment of various inflammatory cells, including Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages, MHCII+ cells, and 1A8+ neutrophils (red corresponds to Nano-11, green to specific cell markers, blue to nuclei). Intracellular Nano-11 is clearly visible within Mac-2+ and MHCII+ cells, indicating efficient phagocytosis. The bottom row, representing soluble OVA injection, shows few inflammatory cells. This figure demonstrates that Nano-11 induces a transient local inflammatory response characterized by immune cell recruitment and that these cells efficiently take up the Nano-11-antigen complexes.